## Docker

A macOS app cannot run in a Linux container, so Docker never runs the app: the window, the Rust build and the bundle are always made on this Mac. The `Dockerfile` is a Linux toolchain (Node.js 24 + Rust + the WebKitGTK libraries Tauri compiles against on Linux, user `dev`); `docker-compose.yml` mounts the project at `/app` and keeps `node_modules`, `src-tauri/target` and the cargo registry in named volumes, so Linux builds never mix with the Mac's. `.dockerignore` sends no build context (the image copies nothing).
{% if choices.docker == "full" %}
Mode: **toolchain in Docker**. The `dev` service runs the Vite dev server on `0.0.0.0:{{ ports.WEB_PORT }}` (published). `npm run dev` on the Mac runs `docker compose up dev` as Tauri's `beforeDevCommand`, waits for it, then compiles and opens the window; hot reload works through the bind mount. `npm run build` runs `docker compose run --rm dev npm run build:web` and bundles `dist/` on the Mac.

```sh
docker compose run --rm dev npm install                  # after cloning or changing dependencies
docker compose run --rm dev npm install <pkg>            # add a UI dependency
docker compose run --rm dev npm run check                # the quality gate (Rust checks run on Linux)
npm run dev                                              # dev window (starts the dev container)
npm run build                                            # .app and .dmg
docker compose build dev                                 # after changing the Dockerfile
docker compose down --volumes --remove-orphans --rmi local   # delete containers, volumes and the image
```

Clippy in the container checks the Linux build of the crate; macOS-only code (`#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]`) is compiled by `npm run build` on the Mac, so run it before finishing such changes.
{%- else %}
Mode: **Docker for checks**. Development, the dev window and builds run on this Mac with Node.js and Rust. `docker compose run --rm --build check` runs `npm ci && npm run check` in a clean Linux container, like CI: use it before releases or when a check might depend on this Mac's setup. The first run builds the image and compiles the Rust dependencies for Linux (a few minutes); the volumes keep later runs fast.

```sh
docker compose run --rm --build check                        # clean install + full quality gate
docker compose down --volumes --remove-orphans --rmi local   # delete the volumes and the image
```

Clippy in the container checks the Linux build of the crate; macOS-only code (`#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]`) is checked by `npm run check` on the Mac.
{%- endif %}
{% endif %}
